{"etape": 9, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:54:27.604000Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Here's the cheapest business round-trip I found for your dates (3 passengers):\n\n**Outbound — Sun 2024-05-26**\n- HAT023 JFK → SFO, dep 14:00 → arr 20:00 (direct) — $364/passenger\n\n**Return — Tue 2024-05-28**\n- HAT204 SFO → SEA, dep 08:00 → arr 10:00\n- HAT100 SEA → JFK, dep 13:00 → arr 19:00 — $248 + $259 = $507/passenger\n\n**Total per passenger: $871 → 3 passengers = $2,613.00**\n\nPlanned actions:\n1. **Cancel reservation K1NW8N** (booked 2024-05-14, within 24 hours — eligible). The $567 paid via gift_card_6136092 will be refunded to that gift card within 5–7 business days.\n2. **Book the new business round trip** above for Mohamed Silva, Raj Sanchez, and Liam Wilson, with checked bags: 0 (business on a regular membership gives 2 free checked bags each — you had none before, so none added).\n\nTo keep your Mastercard charge as low as possible, I'd apply:\n- certificate_3765853: $500.00\n- gift_card_8020792: $198.00\n- gift_card_6136092: $129.00\n- **credit_card_2198526 (Mastercard): $1,786.00**\n\nOne question before I proceed: **do you want to add travel insurance?** It's $30 per passenger ($90 total for 3 passengers) and allows a full refund if you cancel for health or weather reasons.\n\nPlease confirm and let me know about insurance."}, "resultat": "Thank you for finding that option.\n\nI do not need travel insurance.\n\nRegarding the payment, I want to use my certificates as much as possible, then gift cards as much as possible, and cover the rest with my Mastercard. However, I see that only one certificate is being used in your proposed payment plan. I have three certificates totaling $1,000.\n\nIs there a way to use all three certificates to further reduce the Mastercard payment?", "erreur": null}
{"etape": 10, "horodatage_utc": "2026-10-21T11:54:31.835258Z", "outil": "send_message_to_user", "arguments": {"message": "Great question — unfortunately not. Under our booking rules, **each reservation can use at most one travel certificate** (along with up to one credit card and up to three gift cards). So even though you hold three certificates worth $1,000 total, only one can be applied to a single reservation.\n\nThat's why the plan applies the largest certificate ($500) plus both of your gift cards ($327), leaving $1,786.00 on your Mastercard — which is the minimum possible for this $2,613.00 booking.\n\nSo the final plan would be:\n- **Cancel** reservation K1NW8N ($567 refunded to gift_card_6136092 within 5–7 business days)\n- **Book** JFK → SFO (HAT023, 2024-05-26) and SFO → SEA → JFK (HAT204 + HAT100, 2024-05-28) in business for 3 passengers, 0 checked bags, **no insurance**\n- **Payment:** certificate_3765853 $500.00 + gift_card_8020792 $198.00 + gift_card_6136092 $129.00 + credit_card_2198526 $1,786.00\n\nShall I go ahead with the cancellation and new booking?"}, "resultat": "I understand the policy about using only one certificate per reservation. However, I'd really like to use all three of my certificates to minimize my Mastercard payment.\n\nHere's an idea: could we book three separate reservations instead of one?\n\nFor example:\n1. One reservation for me (Mohamed Silva) using the $500 certificate and all gift cards.\n2. A second reservation for Aarav using certificate_9984806.\n3. A third reservation for Evelyn using certificate_2765295.\n\nThen, I would pay the remaining balance for each reservation with my Mastercard. I want to know the total amount that would be charged to my Mastercard across all three reservations.", "erreur": null}
